{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_onn7q3wyalwqdlkbnikooceqnxsgljc2pg43acqg2yvtqn5cde3q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01T8b7sGtMGPJiSu3eo8GwgY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> CONFIGS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Result\n\n```\n$ cargo build && cargo test --test phase_b_configs\nrunning 38 tests\n...\ntest result: ok. 38 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out\n```\n\nEvery row above passes across its randomized inputs, in all three cargo\nconfigurations (`--no-default-features`, default, `--all-features` — identical\nby construction, see `SYMBOLS.md`) and against both the dev-profile and the\nrelease-profile Rust `.so` (`scripts/verify.sh`).\n\n## Note on the reference C build\n\n`c_src/CMakeLists.txt` sets no `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`, so the reference `.so` is\nbuilt at `-O0`, where gcc emits the three function-local `static const` tables\nin declaration order:\n\n```\n.rodata +0    g_scf_long   (184 B)\n        +184  padding      (8 B, zeros)\n        +192  g_scf_short  (320 B)\n        +512  g_scf_mixed  (320 B)   -> .rodata ends at +832\n```\n\n`src/lib.rs` reproduces exactly this layout, which is what makes rows 22-24\n(the `sr_idx == 8` out-of-bounds table rows) byte-identical. For the record,\ngcc **reverses** the order at `-O1` and above (`mixed`, `short`, `long`), so the\nC's own out-of-bounds reads are not stable across optimisation levels — see the\nnote at the end of `ERRORS.md`.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'PY'\np='ERRORS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nrow23 = \"\"\"| 23 | `read_side_info` | **unaligned** `bs_t *` and `L3_gr_info_t *` (pointers skewed by 1..7 bytes) — the C has no alignment requirement enforcement and x86-64 loads/stores tolerate it | identical outputs to the aligned case; no fault | `err_23_unaligned_pointers` |\n\"\"\"\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"| 22 | `read_side_info` | out-of-range \"enum\" values\"\"\", row23 + \"\"\"| 22 | `read_side_info` | out-of-range \"enum\" values\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"## Note on row 16\"\"\", \"\"\"## Result\n\nAll 23 rows have a passing differential test:\n\n```\n$ cargo build && cargo test --test phase_c_errors\nrunning 23 tests\n...\ntest result: ok. 23 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out\n```\n\n## Note on row 16\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\ngrep -c '^| ' ERRORS.md; grep -n 'err_23' ERRORS.md","description":"Append results to CONFIGS.md and add row 23 to ERRORS.md"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1164,"cache_read_input_tokens":165209,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1164,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e36a5fd1-af0c-40dd-ba1d-527712909c23","uuid":"1fd61e10-ad1a-47e4-bf1d-f041c701134a","timestamp":"2026-08-19T14:41:46.227Z"}
