{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_3bkd7nqz7dirg5y3n3dx2jyrgyre6thsobvr6oti2prih3nz6gjq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete and green. Summary:\n\n## What the library is\nA single C translation unit (`c_src/src/lib.c`, 163 lines) exporting one symbol — `read_side_info`, the MP3 side-info parser from minimp3 — plus the file-local `get_bits` helper and three `static const` scalefactor-band tables.\n\n## Phase A artifacts (all derived mechanically from the C)\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | `nm -D` surface: C exports exactly `read_side_info`; Rust exports it too. **No `[features]` exist in `Cargo.toml` and no `#[cfg(feature=…)]` in `src/`**, so the feature power set is `{∅}`; all three cargo spellings verified. |\n| `ERRORS.md` | **23 rows**, one per distinct rejection: the 3 `return -1` branches, `get_bits`' truncation early-out, both `>` vs `>=` boundaries, negative/zero/overflowing `pos`/`limit`, the `limit + mdb*8` signed-overflow wrap, the unchecked `sr_idx == 8` OOB table row, all four null-pointer inputs, unaligned pointers, and the \"no enums exist\" analysis. |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | **38 rows** covering the cross-product the C actually branches on: MPEG1/2 layout × mono/stereo (`gr_count` 1/2/4) × `sr_idx` 0–8 × window-switching × `block_type` 1/2/3 × `mixed_block_flag` × per-granule heterogeneity × all 8 start alignments × negative/deep `pos` × tight/exact/short `limit` × value boundaries. |\n\n## Phases B–D\n- **66 tests** (`tests/phase_b_configs.rs` 38, `phase_c_errors.rs` 23, `phase_d_symbols.rs` 5), all loading **both** `.so`s via `libloading` and calling only the exported symbol. Every call compares the return value, `bs->pos`/`bs->limit`, and all 32 bytes of all six `L3_gr_info_t` slots (pointer field via cross-granule deltas + pointed-to table bytes; sentinel pre-fill makes \"the C never writes this field\" an asserted property).\n- All green under every feature spelling **and** against the release `.so`; `nm -D` diff is empty for both profiles. `scripts/verify.sh` reproduces everything from scratch.\n\n## Findings / fixes\n- `src/lib.rs` needed **no behavioural fix** — 15 injected mutations confirmed the harness detects divergence (14/15; the miss is the one irreproducible case below).\n- Two real harness-level parity issues found and fixed in `Cargo.toml`: `crate-type` needed `rlib` added so `cargo test` actually builds/freshens the cdylib under test, and `[profile.dev] debug-assertions = false` because rustc's UB-checks made a null `bs_t*` abort (SIGABRT) where the C faults (SIGSEGV) — all four null-pointer tests now match exactly.\n- One documented, unmatchable case: `&g_scf_mixed[8]` (reachable when `sr_idx == 8`) reads past the end of the C's `.rodata` into link-time unwind data. The Rust reproduces the reference `-O0` table layout so the `long`/`short` row-8 aliases match byte-for-byte, and supplies zeros beyond; only those 40 bytes are exempt from comparison (everything else, including the pointer offset, is asserted)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":545,"cache_read_input_tokens":195582,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":545,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e36a5fd1-af0c-40dd-ba1d-527712909c23","uuid":"07b3d09a-bb33-49dd-97d0-1a89292cbbff","timestamp":"2026-08-19T14:45:49.453Z"}
